(Regression test for whole-list printing - plan 000 / COLLECTIONS_ROADMAP.
 Previously `print mylist.` printed the raw heap pointer instead of the
 list's contents. Now a per-tag dispatch renders [elem, elem, ...], text
 elements are quoted so ["1"] is distinguishable from [1], empty lists
 print [], and inline {mylist} interpolation renders the same way.)

(Homogeneous integer list)
a list called nums is [1, 2, 3].
print nums.

(Homogeneous text list - elements quoted)
a list called names is ["Alice", "Bob"].
print names.

(Mixed list - each element rendered by its own runtime tag)
a list called m is [1, "two", 3.5, yes].
print m.

(Empty list)
a list called blank is [].
print blank.

(Inline format interpolation)
print "list: {nums}".

(Homogeneous float list)
a list called vals is [1.5, 2.5].
print vals.

(Homogeneous boolean list - renders as 1/0)
a list called flags is [yes, no, yes].
print flags.

(Single element - no separator)
a list called single is [7].
print single.

(Appended list - exercises _list_append tag writes then _list_print)
a list called acc is [1, 2].
append 3 to acc.
print acc.

(Retagged slot - set element retags, whole-list print reflects it)
set element 1 of m to "one".
print m.

(Edge cases: strings with spaces stay quoted, negative integers render,
 and an empty list interpolates inline as [])
a list called greet is ["hello world", "foo"].
print greet.
a list called negs is [-5, 3].
print negs.
print "empty inline: {blank}".